title: Left-wing Split
new-page: true
subtitle: The Left's disagreements with our policies have grown too severe.
tags: event
view-if: not left_split and ((spd_centrist and left_dissent >= 70) or (not spd_centrist and left_dissent >= 60))
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_split = 1;
Q.left_strength = Q.left_strength / 2;
Q.workers_spd -= 5;
Q.unemployed_spd -= 5;
Q.workers_other += 5;
Q.workers_kpd += 3;
Q.rb_strength -= 300;
Q.kpd_relation -= 5;
if (Q.rb_militancy >= 0.1) Q.rb_militancy -= 0.05;
dropAdvisors("left", ["levi", "sender", "rosenfeld", "seydewitz", "siemsen"], 0);
!}
go-to: sapd_formed if centrists_resign = 1 and not sapd_formed

= Left-wing members split

Our policy choices have greatly offended the left, and many of their leaders have split to form a new party, the SAPD, or Socialist Workers' Party. They do not count a huge section of our membership, so this should be survivable.

[? if centrists_resign = 1 : Many former Centrist Marxists have joined with the SAPD, the party formed by dissident leftists. They have brought their support base and organization skills to the party, leading to its growth as a nascent rival to the SPD for the support of the working class. ?]